.TH PERROR 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
perror \- print an error message to standard error
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <stdio.h>
.B void perror(const char *prefix);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints the message for the current errno to Crunch standard error, followed
by a newline. A nonempty prefix is followed by a colon and space.
The messages are those supplied by
.BR strerror (3crunch).
The original errno is preserved even if output fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR strerror (3crunch),
.BR fputs (3crunch)
